Mupen64Plus for RISC OS
=======================

A Nintendo 64 emulator: mupen64plus 2.6 (core, Rice video, HLE RSP, SDL audio and input),
ported to RISC OS 5. It draws with OpenGL through Andy Youll's RISC3D, on the GPU where
RISC3D has one.

Playing a game
--------------
Drop an N64 ROM on the icon bar icon: a .z64, .v64 or .n64 file, or a zip holding one.
The game opens in a desktop window; Alt+Enter switches to full screen and back. Clicking
the icon offers the last game played again. Close the window, or press Escape, to stop.

While a game runs, the icon's menu has its commands too: Save state, Load state, Slot (0-9,
the ticked one is in use), Full screen, Pause and Stop game. The game's window can cover the
icon bar: Shift+F12 brings it forward.

You need your own ROMs: dump the cartridges you own. None come with this program.

Keys (controller 1)
-------------------
  Arrow keys   analogue stick          Return       Start
  Left Shift   A                       Left Ctrl    B
  Z            Z trigger               X / C        L / R
  W A S D      D-pad                   I J K L      C buttons
The window must have the input focus (click on it). Other keys:
  Escape       stop                    P            pause
  F5 / F7      save / load state       0-9          state slot
  F9           reset                   Insert       screenshot (into !Mupen64Plus.Screenshots)
  F           fast forward             Y            speed limiter on/off

Settings and saves
------------------
Choices... on the icon's menu sets the window size, full screen at the start, the emulation
(the dynamic recompiler is the fast one) and sound. They apply from the next game. Its Edit
file button opens all the settings: mupen64plus/cfg, a text file. Edit it between games, as
the emulator writes it when a game ends (it keeps the save state slot there).

All of it is in <Choices$Write>.Mupen64Plus: mupen64plus/cfg (the settings), Saves (game
saves and save states), and stdout and stderr (the emulator's log).

Needs
-----
- RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 machine with VFPv3 (a Raspberry Pi 2 or later), or RISC OS on Linux,
  or RoMac.
- For OpenGL: !RISC3D in !Boot.Resources (0.22 or later on a Pi 4; restart after installing
  it). It's from https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-risc3d/releases. !MesaLibs isn't needed:
  the OpenGL libraries are built in.
- SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (from PackMan).
- For sound: SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager in !System. Without them it's silent.
- About 200 MB of free memory.

Known limits
------------
- On a Pi 4 with a RISC3D older than 0.22, games stop with "Failed to allocate device memory
  for BO" unless !MesaLibs is in !Boot.Resources too. Update RISC3D, or install !MesaLibs, and
  restart.
- Use a 16M colour desktop mode. In a 64K colour mode the game's picture comes out garbled
  (riscos-mesa's OpenGL window code, reported).
- No joystick yet: the keyboard only.
- Alt+Enter also presses Start in the game (Return is Start).
- Full screen at a window size the screen has no mode for (960 x 720, say) shows the picture
  in a corner of the nearest bigger mode.

